# Comparison of LAMMPS pair gcpm against the GCPM Fortran code
#
# Workflow:
#   1) build the compare-instrumented Fortran (adds dump_compare.f):
#        gfortran -O2 -fno-automatic -ffixed-line-length-132 -w \
#          main.f init.f force.f Pos_alc.f pre_corrc_average.f \
#          diel_cerf_hbond.f dump_compare.f -o md_water_cmp
#   2) run it (needs param, pwat1.dat, pwatin) -> writes frame.dat + eforce.dat
#        ./md_water_cmp
#   3) convert the frame to a LAMMPS data file:
#        python3 pwatin_to_lammps.py frame.dat data.gcpm
#   4) run this input and compare the printed energies to eforce.dat.
#
# GCPM parameters are taken from MD_water/param:
#   epsilon = 110 K = 0.218445 kcal/mol, sigma = 3.69 Ang, gamma(buck) = 12.75
#   M-site Gaussian width 0.610, H width 0.455, polarizability 1.444 Ang^3
#   reaction-field dielectric 78.4 (hard-coded in the Fortran), cutoff = rcut.
# The exp-6 dispersion acts between O sites (type 1) only; H/M have epsilon = 0.
#
# Compare the output between LAMMPS and Fortran at the first timestep (run 0)
#   evdwl  <->  E_disp   (exp-6, no tail)        -- matches to ~5 digits
#   pe     <->  E_total  (uconf, no tail)        -- offset by the cutoff
#                                                   convention (molecular vs
#                                                   atomic) + RF self/intra
#                                                   bookkeeping; see below.
#
# Useful isolations:
#  * dispersion only:        keep as is, compare evdwl to E_disp.
#  * pure smeared Coulomb:   pair_style gcpm 0 0.0 ${rc} ${rc}
#                            and add  'neigh_modify exclude molecule/intra all'
#                            then compare ecoul to E_coul_smear.
#
# Known differences (not bugs, see src/GCPM/gcpm_lammps_vs_fortran.md):
#  - Fortran truncates by molecule COM-COM distance; LAMMPS by atom-atom
#    distance. This shifts charge-charge (offset H/M sites) at the cutoff shell;
#    dispersion (O ~ at COM) is unaffected, hence its near-exact match.
#  - Fortran sums intermolecular Coulomb + explicit RF self terms; the LAMMPS
#    per-pair RF gets the self terms from intramolecular pairs instead.
#  - Fortran adds an analytic exp-6 tail (eset); LAMMPS uses pair_modify shift/tail.

variable equil_steps     index 1000
variable relax_steps     index 1000
variable datafile  index data.gcpm
variable r         index 1

variable T         index 298
variable P         index 1.0         # 1 atm = 0.101 MPa

variable velseed   index 817324
variable seed      index 576211

# cutoff must equal the Fortran rcut printed at startup (e.g. 11.220684 Ang)
variable rc        index 11.220684

units real
atom_style hybrid full dipole sphere
